# Ephara's Dispersal: "This spell costs {2} less to cast if it targets an attacking creature" (CR 601.2f). Bot1 attacks with
# one of its two Grizzly Bears on turn 3. With only Mox Sapphire's {U}, Bot2 cannot cast it at the Bear that stayed home
# ({2}{U}), but can at the attacker for {U} (pool empty right after). The attacker returns to Bot1's hand, so no damage
# is dealt, then Bot2 surveils 2: one card goes to the graveyard and the other stays on top (the card is what the
# surveil sees, in order).

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Emerald
Grizzly Bears
Grizzly Bears
Island x3
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Ephara's Dispersal
Island x5
Forest
Mountain
Island x12

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Grizzly Bears.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Grizzly Bears.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Grizzly Bears#1 > Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
! Bot2.Hand.Ephara's Dispersal.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Grizzly Bears#2; Mana: short)
Bot2.Hand.Ephara's Dispersal.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Grizzly Bears#1)
? Bot2.Mana =
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Arrange(Island | Mountain)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 2
Bot1.Hand.Grizzly Bears.Power = 2
Bot2.Life = 20
Bot2.Graveyard = Ephara's Dispersal; Mountain
Bot2.Library = Island; Island; Island; Island; Island; Island; Island; Island; Island; Island; Island; Island
